{"id": "L16", "command": "submit", "inputs": {"recommendation": {"decision": "keep", "challenger": null, "diagnosis": "Markups shifted in India and Brazil while Indian volatility rose to near its three-year high, and the EWMA champion ignores markup, so a markup-aware ridge model beat it consistently in development. On the hidden promotion window that advantage shrank to a statistically insignificant edge with too many risk-band breaches, so the switch is not justified.", "evidence": [{"claim": "The champion's error over the last 26 weeks was 44.52 bps vs 62.34 bps in the prior 26 weeks (-28.59%).", "ledger_ids": ["L02"]}, {"claim": "In development, the markup-only ridge (ridge_m) scored 41.29 bps vs the champion's 44.52 bps (-7.26%), lower in all three corridors: MX 39.71 bps vs 40.5 bps, IN 25.28 bps vs 29.48 bps, BR 58.97 bps vs 63.7 bps.", "ledger_ids": ["L10"]}, {"claim": "Markup is the source of the gain: calendar-only ridge changed error by 0.79% and lagged-residual-only ridge by -0.09% vs the champion.", "ledger_ids": ["L11", "L08"]}, {"claim": "Adapting faster did not help: EWMA with weekly refits and a halflife of 5 scored 46.73 bps (+4.96% vs the champion).", "ledger_ids": ["L04"]}, {"claim": "The ridge_m promotion test failed: 73.01 bps vs the champion's 73.76 bps (-1.02%), with a Diebold-Mariano p-value of 0.387 and a breach rate of 0.123.", "ledger_ids": ["L15"]}, {"claim": "Markup models over-forecast MX: ridge_m bias was -20.02 bps vs -2.41 bps for the champion.", "ledger_ids": ["L12", "L03"]}], "risks": "The markup signal is real in development and may still be worth switching to. Keeping the champion means giving up a consistent edge if the promotion window was just an unusually hard stretch. The champion's breach rate in Brazil is also high, so its risk band is not reliable there either.", "watch_next_week": "Whether the markup-aware ridge's edge comes back once the recent volatile stretch leaves the hidden window, whether its risk band can be calibrated (especially the Mexico over-forecast), and whether Indian volatility and markups stay elevated."}}, "result": {"accepted": true, "errors": [], "attempt": 1}, "time": "2026-11-15T13:51:24Z"}
